    <Folder>
      <name>Eucalyptus </name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>245.0</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Genus Species: Eucalyptus mannifera<br>Common Name: Brittle Gum<br>Height: 20<br>Crown Radius: 11<br>DBH: 106<br>Tree Age: Mature<br>SIGNIFICANCE: Exceptional<br>Tree Health: Fair<br>Tree Structure: Fair<br>ULE: 15 to 25<br>Habitat: Yes<br>Classification: Other eucalyptus<br>GPS COORDS: -35.2899005561 149.117585409<br>Comments: 1916 original planting tracing the old alignment of Balmain crescent towards Lennox Crossing. Cavity + lots of smaller hollows<br>OTHER OBSERVATIONS: bird damage,cavity,high codominant,previous failures,wound,secondary shooting]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1739-1A237E</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
